  <prompt>Implement the H13 E2E acceptance-gate handler as an IJobHandler in the L2 control-plane. H13 invokes the extended scripts/Validate-DeployedEnvironment.ps1 (Phase B) and asserts EFFECTS not intentions (per R7). Checks: BFF /health, sample analysis, sample document upload+index, workspace-layout render, wizard field-map, ALL 6 §4B T1–T6 silent-fail traps cleared, ALL 5 §4D I1–I5 tenant-isolation invariants sample-verified, `scripts/naming-conformance-check.ps1` exit 0 on r1-owned surfaces, cost envelope conforms per §15 #14. Registry `Setup Status` transitions to `Ready` ONLY if H13 exits 0. Idempotency key: validate-{customerId}-{buildId}.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in IJobHandler contract, E2E acceptance validation, effect-verification pattern (R7 — assert effects not intentions), all §4B silent-fail traps + §4D tenant-isolation invariants, cost-envelope drift detection, naming-conformance gate. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>File src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Handlers/H13E2EAcceptanceGateHandler.cs exists, implements IJobHandler, registers in L2 DI, and: (a) invokes extended Validate-DeployedEnvironment.ps1 with all sample checks (BFF /health + sample analysis + sample doc upload+index + workspace-layout render + wizard field-map); (b) invokes each of 6 T1–T6 trap verifications (T1 keyVaultReferenceIdentity, T2 Dataverse App User, T3 Graph app-role parity, T4 Exchange policies count == 2, T5 both-slot MI KV RBAC OR UAMI structural, T6 SPE confidential-client used); (c) sample-verifies each of 5 I1–I5 tenant-isolation invariants; (d) invokes `scripts/naming-conformance-check.ps1` — must exit 0 on r1-owned surfaces; (e) queries Azure Cost Management for the customer stamp and asserts cost envelope per §15 #14; (f) ONLY on ALL green does Dataverse registry `Setup Status` transition to Ready; (g) asserts idempotency key validate-{customerId}-{buildId}. Unit tests cover happy path (all green → Ready), each trap-fail branch (Ready NOT set), each invariant-fail branch, naming-conformance-fail, cost-drift-fail (per §14 threshold), and idempotency.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Per spec.md FR-18 + SC #5, #6, #17 + design.md §4.1 H13 + §4B trap catalog + §4D invariant catalog: H13 is the FINAL gate. Registry Setup Status transitions to Ready ONLY if H13 exits 0. Validates every prior handler's post-condition + every §4D invariant + naming + cost. Cost drift > 20% is currently ambiguous (fail-run or advisory per spec.md Unresolved Questions) — implement as advisory-warn by default with explicit escalation trigger on 20%+ (owner to confirm).</background>
