  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0">Declare rigor level (FULL) and load knowledge files.</step>
    <step order="1">Author H13E2EAcceptanceGateHandler.cs — inject IPowerShellRunner, ITrapVerifier (per T1–T6), IInvariantSampler (per I1–I5), INamingConformanceRunner, IAzureCostClient, IDataverseRegistryClient, IIdempotencyService, ICosmosRunStore.</step>
    <step order="2">Invoke extended Validate-DeployedEnvironment.ps1 for sample E2E checks (health, analysis, doc upload+index, layout render, field-map).</step>
    <step order="3">Invoke each of 6 T1–T6 trap verifiers independently; short-circuit-collect failures into diagnostic list.</step>
    <step order="4">Sample-verify each of 5 I1–I5 invariants; short-circuit-collect failures.</step>
    <step order="5">Invoke `scripts/naming-conformance-check.ps1`; assert exit 0 on r1-owned surfaces.</step>
    <step order="6">Query Azure Cost Management for the customer stamp; compare to expected envelope per §15 #14; flag cost drift &gt; 20% (advisory-warn default; owner-configurable to fail-run per spec.md Unresolved Questions).</step>
    <step order="7">If ALL checks green: transition Dataverse registry sprk_dataverseenvironment.SetupStatus → Ready + clear sprk_currentrunid. If ANY check fails: Cosmos state = Quarantined per §4C; do NOT transition Setup Status.</step>
    <step order="8">Author unit tests: (a) all green → Ready, (b) each T1–T6 trap fail branch (6 tests) → Quarantined, (c) each I1–I5 invariant fail branch (5 tests) → Quarantined, (d) naming-conformance non-zero → Quarantined, (e) cost drift &gt; 20% → advisory or fail per config, (f) idempotency.</step>
    <step order="9">Register in L2 Program.cs DI.</step>
    <step order="10">Run dotnet build + dotnet test; verify green + zero analyzer warnings.</step>
    <step order="11">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change task 055 status from 🔲 to ✅.</step>
    <step order="12">Document any deviations in projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If ANY of the 6 T1–T6 traps fails, STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 rather than retry-looping — trap failure indicates upstream handler regression, root cause required (not a transient).</trigger>
    <trigger>If ANY of the 5 I1–I5 invariants fails at sample verification, STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 — invariant fail is CATASTROPHIC severity per §4D (cross-tenant bleed risk).</trigger>
    <trigger>If cost drift &gt; 20% is detected per §15 #14 (SC #14), STOP and escalate to confirm advisory-vs-fail semantics per spec.md Unresolved Questions — do NOT silently transition to Ready over cost drift.</trigger>
    <trigger>If naming-conformance-check.ps1 finds violations on r1-owned surfaces (Phase G regression), STOP and escalate — do NOT accept the drift.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Closest neighbor: scripts/Validate-DeployedEnvironment.ps1 (existing; Phase B extends). scripts/naming-conformance-check.ps1 (r3 task 063). No existing L2 handler that composes trap + invariant + naming + cost verification.</existing>
    <extension>No — H13 is the SOLE authoritative gate for Setup Status = Ready. Extending Validate-DeployedEnvironment.ps1 alone cannot own Cosmos state transitions + §4C Quarantined semantics + Dataverse registry transition — those require an IJobHandler.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without H13 as the sole Setup Status = Ready gatekeeper, registry rows could transition to Ready with silent trap failures still present (T1 keyVaultReferenceIdentity mismatch → BFF boots with null KV refs → runtime failures the moment operator hands the env to customer). H13 is the r1 acceptance floor.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test .NET projects</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">az CLI for cost queries</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Handlers/H13E2EAcceptanceGateHandler.cs</output>
    <output type="test">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Handlers/H13E2EAcceptanceGateHandler.Tests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given ALL upstream handlers succeeded, ALL 6 T1–T6 traps clear, ALL 5 I1–I5 invariants clear, naming-conformance exit 0, cost envelope conforms — when HandleAsync runs, then Dataverse registry sprk_dataverseenvironment.SetupStatus transitions to Ready AND sprk_currentrunid is cleared.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Extended Validate-DeployedEnvironment.ps1 asserts EFFECTS (per R7): BFF /health returns 200; sample analysis returns success; sample doc upload+index returns success; workspace-layout render succeeds; wizard field-map returns expected mapping.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Trap verification (spec.md SC #6): each of T1 (App Service keyVaultReferenceIdentity == UAMI), T2 (systemusers filter returns 1), T3 (UAMI SP appRoleAssignments == all 14 in GraphAppRoles.cs), T4 (Get-ApplicationAccessPolicy returns 2 entries with matching principals), T5 (both slot MIs KV RBAC OR UAMI-structural post-Phase-C), T6 (SPE container-type creation used confidential-client per creation-audit) is independently re-verified.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Invariant verification (spec.md §4D sample-verify): I1 grep provisioning scripts for tenant-shaped GUID defaults returns none; I2 sample AI Search query per index has tenantId filter; I3 sample Cosmos query has partition-key predicate; I4 SPE container-ID resolution goes through ITenantContainerResolver; I5 Graph token acquisition includes explicit tenantId.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Naming (spec.md SC #17): scripts/naming-conformance-check.ps1 exits 0 on r1-owned surfaces; H13 fails deploy with "NamingConformanceFailed" otherwise.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cost envelope (spec.md SC #14 + §15 #14): Azure Cost Management report against expected; deviations &gt; 20% flagged (advisory-warn OR fail per configured semantic).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Rollback (spec.md §4C): given ANY of T1–T6 or I1–I5 or naming or cost checks fails, when HandleAsync runs, then Cosmos state = Quarantined AND Setup Status is NOT transitioned to Ready AND sprk_currentrunid is retained (blocks new runs).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Idempotency: two invocations for the same customerId + buildId — second call is a no-op (validate-{customerId}-{buildId} match); no re-verification if idempotency-key matches AND registry status is Ready.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: H13 invoked without tenantId parameter returns failure (§4D I1); all sample queries per-tenant scoped.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Handler registers in L2 DI; dotnet build + dotnet test exit 0; zero analyzer warnings.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Reference: spec.md FR-18 + SC #5, #6, #14, #17 + §4D I1..I5 + MUST rules; design.md §4.1 H13 (final gate) + §4B (all traps) + §4C (Quarantined semantics on failure) + §4D (invariants) + §15 #14 (cost). H13 is the FINAL handler in the DAG and the sole authority for Setup Status = Ready. Phase A + Phase B + all prior Wave C4 handlers + Wave C6 ArchTests must land before H13 can run end-to-end.</notes>

